 2,500 - AED 12,000 per m\\\\u00b2\\\", \\\"address\\\": {\\\"@type\\\": \\\"PostalAddress\\\", \\\"streetAddress\\\": \\\"Jebel Ali Industrial Area 1\\\", \\\"addressLocality\\\": \\\"Dubai\\\", \\\"addressCountry\\\": \\\"AE\\\"}, \\\"geo\\\": {\\\"@type\\\": \\\"GeoCoordinates\\\", \\\"latitude\\\": 24.9857, \\\"longitude\\\": 55.0272}, \\\"openingHoursSpecification\\\": {\\\"@type\\\": \\\"OpeningHoursSpecification\\\", \\\"dayOfWeek\\\": [\\\"Monday\\\", \\\"Tuesday\\\", \\\"Wednesday\\\", \\\"Thursday\\\", \\\"Friday\\\", \\\"Saturday\\\"], \\\"opens\\\": \\\"09:00\\\", \\\"closes\\\": \\\"18:00\\\"}, \\\"areaServed\\\": [\\\"Dubai\\\", \\\"Abu Dhabi\\\", \\\"United Arab Emirates\\\", \\\"Saudi Arabia\\\", \\\"Qatar\\\", \\\"Kuwait\\\", \\\"Bahrain\\\", \\\"Oman\\\"]}\"}}]\n10:Tce3,<h1>Indoor vs Outdoor LED Screen: Which Do You Need in Dubai?</h1><p>Blog — Indoor Vs Outdoor Led Screen Dubai. Premium LED display solutions by Brightluxx in Dubai, UAE.</p><p>Brightness, IP rating, pixel pitch and cost — the practical differences between indoor and outdoor LED screens for Dubai projects, and how to choose.</p><div><h2>The 60-second answer</h2><p>Choose an <strong>outdoor LED screen in Dubai</strong> when the display faces direct sunlight or weather: you need 5,000+ nits brightness, IP65 sealing and coarser pitch (P4–P10). Choose an <strong>indoor LED screen</strong> for lobbies, retail and boardrooms: 600–1,200 nits is enough, no weather sealing needed, and budgets go into finer pixel pitch (P1.2–P2.5) for close viewing.</p><h2>Brightness: Dubai sun changes everything</h2><p>Dubai's direct sun demands 5,000–8,000 nits for legible daytime content; indoor screens at 800 nits would look switched off outdoors. Conversely, running an outdoor panel indoors wastes money and blinds viewers — auto-dimming helps but the panel cost is already spent.</p><h2>IP rating and Dubai's climate</h2><p>Outdoor panels need IP65 front and rear against dust storms, humidity and 50°C summers, with conformal-coated boards for coastal salt air. Indoor panels are typically IP30 and lighter, enabling slimmer cabinets and easier mounting.</p><h2>Pixel pitch and viewing distance</h2><p>Outdoor audiences are far away, so P6–P10 looks perfect from 20m+ at a fraction of fine-pitch cost. Indoor viewers stand 2–6m away, needing P1.2–P2.5. Use our <a href=\"/viewing-distance\">viewing distance calculator</a> to match pitch to your audience.</p><h2>Cost comparison</h2><p>Per square metre, outdoor screens run AED 3,900–9,500 and indoor fine-pitch from AED 7,500 — full ranges in our <a href=\"/blog/led-display-pricing-guide-uae\">UAE pricing guide</a>. Outdoor projects add structure, cranage and DEWA power works; indoor projects add wall preparation and processing.</p><h2>Semi-outdoor: the middle case</h2><p>Window-facing displays behind glass (mall shopfronts, car showrooms) need 3,500+ nits to beat glass reflection but not full IP65 — a distinct specification many suppliers get wrong. Our <a href=\"/glassmorph\">transparent LED range</a> is built exactly for this case.</p><p>Still unsure? Browse <a href=\"/indoor-led\">indoor LED</a> and <a href=\"/outdoor-led\">outdoor LED</a> ranges, or ask our <a href=\"/dubai\">LED display company in Dubai</a> — send a photo of your location and we'll specify it the same day.</p></div><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Can I use an indoor LED screen outdoors in Dubai?</h3><p>No — indoor panels lack the brightness (5,000+ nits needed), IP65 weather sealing and thermal design for Dubai's sun, dust and heat. They fail quickly and look washed out in daylight.</p><h3>What brightness do I need for an outdoor LED screen in Dubai?</h3><p>5,000–8,000 nits for direct-sun locations, with automatic ambient dimming at night to comply with RTA limits for road-facing screens.</p><h3>Which is cheaper, indoor or outdoor LED?</h3><p>Per square metre, outdoor coarse-pitch screens (AED 3,900–9,500/m²) are usually cheaper than indoor fine-pitch (from AED 7,500/m²), but outdoor projects add structural steel, cranage and power works.</p>3:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$10\"}}]\n4:[\"$\",\"$L11\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$12\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@13\"}]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L15\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$12\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Blog — Indoor Vs Outdoor Led Screen Dubai | Brightluxx\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Blog — Indoor Vs Outdoor Led Screen Dubai. Premium LED display solutions by Brightluxx in Dubai, UAE.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://brightluxx.com/blog/indoor-vs-outdoor-led-screen-dubai\"}]]}]}]}],null]}]\n9:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L16\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L17\",null,{}]}]]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/00m338-wepjwk.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\"}],[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/3ai24x07kh91w.js\",\"async\":true}]],[\"$\",\"html\",null,{\"lang\":\"en\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"body\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"$L16\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L17\",null,{}],\"notFound\":[[\"$\",\"main\",null,{\"className\":\"not-found\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"children\":\"404 — Page Not Found\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The page you requested does not exist.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/products\",\"children\":\"Browse product